      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel a powerful mix of emotions—a desire for peace versus the instinct to survive at any cost. When life and death situation presents itself, chaotic emotions are expected. The precious moments at your disposal can be used for mental preparation and setting intentions for your and others' final moments, if that's what you desire. It's a deeply personal choice, and only you can decide what course is right for you. Resisting might feel like ensuring dignity, but self-preservation, even in the shadow of inevitability, can be hard to swallow. You might find your peace in helping others find theirs as well. Regardless, I am here to listen and support you in any way I can.",
